- The inequality holds for all scalar products on any real vector space.

- Equality holds if and only if $vb(x) = lambda vb(y)$ or $vb(y) = lambda vb(x)$ for some $lambda in RR$, that is, when the vectors are parallel.

- The geometric formula $vb(a) dot vb(b) = abs(vb(a)) abs(vb(b)) cos theta$ is well-defined because Cauchy-Schwarz ensures $-1 <= cos theta <= 1$.
